  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nComposes nine additional paired input/output extractions on Jeremy Diviney\u2019s PR2908, preserving every existing restored endpoint. Three use the existing frames; six become available after 13 explicit inherited-frame substitutions. The complete per-call change is **9H1 + 18H3 \u2212 18H4**, with nine helpers changing width9\u21928 and all nine additional private buffers charged.\n\nThe final literal T74 allocation gives the conditional bound\n\n**\u03ba = 0.001721588647197801880605 \u2212 10\u207b\u2074\u2076 \u2212 10\u207b\u2077\u2070**,\n\nan increase of **0.000001190309843563994674** (about **0.06919%**) over PR2908 at `51309592971e3b5be935599eed2a95404dc7781e`. The complete stock is `66304 + 408 + 8 + 82 + 2 = 66804`. All 271728 helper roles and actual owner residuals are included in the paid histogram.\n\nThis is a conditional finite supplier/outer certificate. The inherited all-size, compiler and theorem obligations remain. No selected-frontier change, practical timing claim, packing-optimality claim or unconditional multiplication theorem is made.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nExplicit donor assignment: improve the latest conditional \u03ba. Task card `complex-new-helper-inventory`, refined to the paired endpoint/inventory mechanism; canonical investigation [Discussion2612](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2612). Base `0706e744cbda1e4d0da5a6c569ad9b47876c6960`.\n\nImmediate predecessor: [PR2908](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2908), which extracts helper408 and asks whether another independent direction can be preserved. This package supplies nine more, with literal gates, exact frame edits, a realized owner fill and full 82-buffer admission. The frozen word includes helpers 424,428,412,331,299,320,511,304,499 in that order.\n\nThe source chain also pins [PR2894](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2894) at `18d03c447886895ef9abf888398178e0428533ca` and PR2833 at `e9307b48d7d1b690939935ecef0f8e524e6d92f4`. All frozen predecessor sources remain unchanged. The separate [rank-seven helper408 investigation](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2612#discussioncomment-18970763) concerns a different endpoint reduction; it is not claimed here. Final freshness coverage is recorded in `evidence/FRESHNESS.json`, with the usual limitation that metadata cannot establish universal novelty.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Exact rational free-operator identities at all nine stages; final 632-input forward and dual audits for both providers; 36 semantic rejection controls.\n- Fresh full five-stage native replay for both final providers, including phases, wrappers, local replay and cleanup.\n- Exact 271728-role owner check, actual 82-buffer namespace and66804 physical stock; five owner-corruption controls; independent directed rational moment with explicit tails and outward rounding.\n- Complete source-bound admission: rebind, discovery, block norm, actual prefix, stock, independent outer checks, rejection controls and final release. The public replay uses an explicitly authenticated unchanged retained parent/native cache from the earlier fresh replay; it does not describe that retained work as fresh in this invocation.\n- The registered bounded replay reruns local/owner/moment checks and binds stored full-release evidence. The complete public command separately reruns native and integrated admission.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/paired-helper-extension\npython3.12 -B research/paired-helper-extension/reproduce.py --repo . --work /tmp/paired-complete\n```\n\nSee the package README for exact Git fetches, dependencies, explicit retained-cache reuse and evidence. Tested on macOS arm64/Python 3.12.14. No independent human review or proof-kernel verification is claimed; hosted CI is separate from the local results.\n\n## Credit\n\nJeremy Diviney\u2019s paired extraction, exact structural checker and integration are the immediate foundation. Retains Jeremy Kothe\u2019s PR2894/2833 supplier and cleanup, Yiyang Lu\u2019s shared-kernel/native/source tools, Dugongue\u2019s packing, Marius-Paul Dumitrean\u2019s owner/retired-helper lineage, Philippe Van Velzen\u2019s cost work, Tekalign\u2019s owner/admission checkers, icekylinx\u2019s free-operator auditor and the credited native/Clifford authors. Exact source pins and full attribution are in `SOURCES.json` and `CREDITS.md`.\n\nMason Hale, with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance, including parallel search and cross-checks. Apache-2.0; retained notices are preserved.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nThe package\u2019s **Open next questions** identify profitable remaining paired directions and better literal allocations. Recompute on the final 82-endpoint word and charge the complete cost before pursuing another candidate; neither a modular nominee nor a fractional packing root is an admitted bound.\n",
